==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhaihta/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|aihta|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|hætta}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hanhtijǭ}}.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|f|hættu|hættur}}

# [[danger]]
# [[hazard]], [[jeopardy]]
# [[peril]]

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-noun-f-w1|h|æ|tt}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|hazard}} [[tvísýna]] {{g|f}}
* {{sense|peril}} [[háski]] {{g|m}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|hætta}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hanhtijaną}}. In the sense “stop” an unstressed prefix has likely been dropped, perhaps {{m|gem-pro|*ab-}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-weak|hætti|hætt}}

# {{context|transitive|governs dative|lang=is}} to [[risk]] (put at risk), [[jeopardize]]
# {{context|ambitransitive|governs dative|lang=is}} to [[quit]], [[stop]], [[cease]], [[cut out]], [[discontinue]]
#: ''Ég '''hætti''' að [[reykja]].''
#:: I '''stopped''' [[smoking]].
#: '''''Hættu'''!''
#:: '''Stop'''!

=====Conjugation=====
{{is-conj-w2|h|æ|tt|mp=-}}

